{"step_index":1118,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:35:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:35:56+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:36:01+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n{\"step_index\":1148,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:35:40Z\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"kill\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"f458c9cf-488d-4cd8-8365-7c4e4b16e3f9/task-1147\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Killing task 1147\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Kill task 1147\\\"\"}}]}\r\n{\"step_index\":1150,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T23:35:44Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Verifying cardinal equality split**\\n\\nThe goal is to show the sum of the cardinality of a ball and its complement equals the total cardinality. The identity `Finset.card_sdiff` helps with the difference of sets. This allows rewriting the equation, simplifying to an equivalent statement. Omega closes the proof immediately.\\n\\n\\n**Bounding radius via eccentricities**\\n\\nDeriving `card ≤ romanWeight f - 2` by relating the cardinality of a filtered set to the roman weight. Deduced `ballWithin G (romanWeight f - 1) u = Finset.univ` by bounding the total set cardinality. Then established `eccentricity G u ≤ romanWeight f - 1` by considering two cases, which leads to `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"cat << 'EOF' > /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_unique_two.lean\\\\nimport Mathlib\\\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\\\n\\\\nopen SimpleGraph\\\\nopen GraphCalc\\\\n\\\\nlemma minUpTo_le {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ n) (hp : p k) :\\\\n    minUpTo n p ≤ k := by\\\\n  unfold minUpTo\\\\n  have hmem : k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p := by\\\\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\\\\n    exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hk, hp⟩\\\\n  have hmin := Finset.min_le hmem\\\\n  generalize hmin_eq : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min = m\\\\n  rw [hmin_eq] at hmin\\\\n  cases m with\\\\n  | top => contradiction\\\\n  | coe val =>\\\\n    simp only [WithTop.coe_le_coe] at hmin\\\\n    exact hmin\\\\n\\\\ntheorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\\\\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\\\\n  unfold GraphCalc.radius\\\\n  have hmem : GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ∈ Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ := by\\\\n    apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\\\\n    exact Finset.mem_univ v\\\\n  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Finset.min_of_mem hmem\\\\n  rw [hb]\\\\n  have hle : (Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ).min ≤ ↑(GraphCalc.eccentricity G v) :=\\\\n    Finset.min_le hmem\\\\n  rw [hb] at hle\\\\n  exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle\\\\n\\\\nlemma mem_ballWithin_of_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] {v w : V} (p : G.Walk v w) :\\\\n    w ∈ ballWithin G p.length v := by\\\\n  induction p using SimpleGraph.Walk.concatRec with\\\\n  | Hnil =>\\\\n    dsimp [ballWithin]\\\\n    exact